    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## HOW RESCHEDULES ARE HANDLED\n\nCalendly sends a reschedule as **two** events:\n1. `invitee.canceled` with `rescheduled = true`\n2. `invitee.created` with `old_invitee` filled in\n\n**Normalize Booking** labels #1 `reschedule_old` and #2 `rescheduled`. The IF node drops #1.\n\nResult: a reschedule is never mistaken for a lost lead, and the lead never gets a \"sorry you cancelled\" email.",
        "height": 284,
        "width": 360,
        "color": 6
      },
      "name": "Sticky · Reschedule Logic",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1328,
        -176
      ],
      "id": "c3b642a0-0738-41cd-9591-694d974f96d7"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## HUBSPOT — CREATE 3 PROPERTIES ONCE\n\nHubSpot → Settings → Properties → Contact → **Create property**. Type **Single-line text** for all three. Internal names must match exactly:\n\n• `meeting_status`\n• `meeting_start_time`\n• `meeting_join_url`\n\n`ai_lead_tier`, `ai_lead_score` and `lead_source_detail` already exist from WF-1.\n\nAfter creating them, click the ↻ refresh icon inside the HubSpot node so n8n sees them.",
        "height": 360,
        "width": 380,
        "color": 6
      },
      "name": "Sticky · HubSpot Properties",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1232,
        336
      ],
      "id": "42f35954-6267-44ea-98ca-744bad327025"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## TEST IT WITH NO BOOKING\n\nThe Calendly Trigger has **pinned test data**: a booking by the same test lead WF-1 uses (`user@example.com`).\n\nClick **Test workflow**. Expected:\n• status `booked`\n• Slack \"CALL BOOKED\" (shows HOT + score if WF-1's test ran first)\n• prep email to the lead\n• one row in the Bookings sheet\n\nCanceled and rescheduled test payloads are in the handover file.",
        "height": 360,
        "width": 360,
        "color": 4
      },
      "name": "Sticky · How To Test",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -32,
        352
      ],
      "id": "39c77fa1-32dd-4fc1-9510-7d1f3f09cd51"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## BOOKINGS SHEET — HEADER ROW\n\nTab name = `cfg_booking_sheet_tab` (default **Bookings**). Row 1 must read exactly:\n\n`Logged At | Status | Name | Email | Meeting | Start (Business TZ) | Invitee Timezone | Join Link | Lead Tier | Lead Score | Known Lead | Canceled By | Cancel Reason | Answers | HubSpot Contact ID | Invitee URI`\n\nMapping mode is **Map Each Column Manually**, so nothing depends on the previous node's output shape.",
        "height": 228,
        "width": 420,
        "color": 4
      },
      "name": "Sticky · Sheet Header",
